      "problem": "Evaluate $\\log_{2} \\left( 2^{5} \\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm reverses the action of the exponent. The idea is that the log of a power of the base equals the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log_b(b^x) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=2$ and $x=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log_{2}\\left( 2^{5}\\right) = 5.\n$$",
